    To reiterate; this lore is [bold][color=#ff0000]Not[/color][/bold] mandatory to follow. It exists here if you do wish to follow the original lore, or want something to work off of.
    There is one major addition to the lore here that (as of writing) would be unique to Ronstation, and in itself, is optional.

    ## Basic rundown
    (Under the original lore,) Most, if not all Shadekin that are employed or under contract from NT are afflicted with a condition they call “Black-eye” and or as the Shadekin themselves refer to as being “Burnt”.
    This affliction and condition supposedly is the cause of them being incapable of returning to “The Dark”.
    Adapted to their home dimension of which is one absent of light, their vision is highly reactive to light levels.
    Dim lights being a source of passive annoyance or discomfort, bright lights ail them much more noticeably, being a source of pain and harm to them.

    ## Silverlining (Ronstation Addition)
    Whilst Shadekin working under NT have been stuck in the Burnout cycle, Nanotrasen, in conjunction with and sponsoring the external group responsible Project PHOENIX, a way to reverse burnout has been found.
    While far from perfect, sometimes causing an initial high pain, it has allowed those with the Black-eye condition to recover and repair their cores, letting them return home. Not all Kin with the Blackeye condition have gone through the operation, and was always intended to be optional.
    Due to the potential of the healing, and the increase in Brighteyes on Stations, Nanotrasen requires any Brighteye Kin (both those recovering from the condition, and those who never had it to begin with) to wear light Nullspace restraints, designed just to prevent phasing while on station premises with as minimal discomfort as possible.
    Testing was done only with willing participants, keeping safety a priority, and the entire process is well documented within Nanotrasen and PHOENIX databanks.

    ## Age & Names
    Shadekin are an example of a very slow biological aging process.
    Whilst maturity and eligible employment are known to standard to be 18.
    Often Shadekin are considered young up until the age range of around 100, the ranges of 100-200 are what would be considered middle-aged, 200-300 being the instance of them starting to enter a elderly state.
    Names are of great significance to Shadekin. Often these names are considered titles and bear them upon entering the physical from their home of “The Dark”.
    These titles are often provided and or given to them by the attributes or qualities they exhibit, however there are other cases where it can be even items, passions, or ideas they are fond of.
    There are instances as well of some Shadekin whom have become acclimated to provide their own titles, replacing previous ones.
    This is not an aspect taken lightly by them nor other Shadekin, such a decision is akin to throwing away their previous selves.
